 Returns `204 No Content` on success.
 
+## Board Publication
+
+Boards are private by default. The `public_url` attribute is `null` until the board is published, then contains its secret public URL. Publishing does not change board membership or `all_access`.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes a board. Only account owners and admins with access to the board can publish it; being the board's creator alone is not sufficient. No request body is required.
+
+Returns `201 Created` with the board JSON, including its `public_url`. Repeated requests keep the same public URL.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes a board. Requires the same permissions as publishing.
+
+Returns `204 No Content`. The old public URL and its nested column and card URLs stop working immediately. Publishing again generates a new secret URL.
+
+### Public pages
+
+Anyone with the secret URL can view these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards belonging to the board are visible; drafts are never public. Invalid or revoked keys, unrelated columns, and unpublished or unrelated cards return `404 Not Found`. Treat the public URL as a secret and only share it with people who should see the board.
+
 ## Board Accesses
 
+
 Board accesses let you see who has access to a board and their involvement level (watching or access only). Any board member can view this information.
 
 ### `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/accesses`
diff --git a/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
